      "name": "jffdougan",
      "username": "jffdougan",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/{size}/1882_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-14T17:44:54.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>OK, in a couple parts:</p><p>- First, after preorder shipping has completed and GtG has finished moving into their new office, are there plans to do a warehouse party to celebrate the release of WCos?</p><p>- If the answer to the above is yes, I would like to propose that, as part of the event, a delegation take a selection of games - including but not limited to SotM - and pay a visit to the children's ward at Barnes (Memorial Hospital). My thoughts are inspired in part by the discussion that happened here:&nbsp;http://boardgamegeek.com/geeklist/182555/item/3596458#item3596458</p><p>I know that St Louis has a pretty well-known children's hospital, and right before I moved to North Carolina the local gaming group had done an event at the local Ronald McDonald house to help brighten up the day of some of its residents. It seems like it would be a good thing to do.</p><p>(mods, please move this to an appropriate forum if deemed appropriate)</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:02.523Z",
