      "id": 123219,
      "name": "Silverleaf",
      "username": "Silverleaf",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-15T20:56:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>My lack of response was due to a lack of being on the right continent, but I like the idea.</p><p>I don't know how things work over the pond, but the thing that would concern me about it would be checking all the necessary child protection boxes - over here you can't just walk into a hospital or school with a bunch of people and some games and interact with children.</p><p>I needed a Criminal Records Bureau (CRB) check (which can take weeks to process) and had to attend child protection training&nbsp;and fill in a lengthy form to sing carols <em>for a couple of hours&nbsp;</em>with children in a hospital with parents, hospital staff, other members of my choir, and my choral director and his wife who are both teachers. Same for teaching children opera and African music.</p><p>This stuff's just not obvious to anyone who hasn't done official volunteering, so I thought I'd point out in case - apologies if you already know about it or this isn't relevant for the US!</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:57:05.129Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
