      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>My lack of response was due to a lack of being on the right continent, but I like the idea.</p><p>I don&#39;t know how things work over the pond, but the thing that would concern me about it would be checking all the necessary child protection boxes - over here you can&#39;t just walk into a hospital or school with a bunch of people and some games and interact with children.</p><p>I needed a Criminal Records Bureau (CRB) check (which can take weeks to process) and had to attend child protection training&nbsp;and fill in a lengthy form to sing carols <em>for a couple of hours&nbsp;</em>with children in a hospital with parents, hospital staff, other members of my choir, and my choral director and his wife who are both teachers. Same for teaching children opera and African music.</p><p>This stuff&#39;s just not obvious to anyone who hasn&#39;t done official volunteering, so I thought I&#39;d point out in case - apologies if you already know about it or this isn&#39;t relevant for the US!</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
